,"original_source":{"page_or_item":"61 FR 64589 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"bbcc990f0250593bf0f990c75861cb29690edb1d1eadfed2783fe7dd4b149ff5","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1996-12-05/pdf/96-31164.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13028#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Section 1 is amended:\n(1) by striking ‘‘and’’ after ‘‘ATDA Act’’ the first time it appears, and\ninserting instead a comma (‘‘,’’);\n(2) by inserting ‘‘, and section 571(a)(1) of Public Law 104–107’’ after\n‘‘FAA’’ the first time it appears; and\n(3) by inserting ‘‘. The functions vested in the President by section\n571(a)(2), (c) and (d) of Public Law 104–107 are also delegated to the\nSecretary, who shall exercise such functions in accordance with recommenda-\ntions of the Council and in consultation with the Secretary of State’’ after\n‘‘State’’ the first time it appears.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"61 FR 64589 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"bbcc990f0250593bf0f990c75861cb29690edb1d1eadfed2783fe7dd4b149ff5","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1996-12-05/pdf/96-31164.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13028#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Section 6 is redesignated as Section 7.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"61 FR 64589 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"bbcc990f0250593bf0f990c75861cb29690edb1d1eadfed2783fe7dd4b149ff5","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1996-12-05/pdf/96-31164.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13028#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) A new Section 6 is added as follows:\n‘‘Sec. 6. Any references in this order to section 571, or any subsection\nof section 571, of Public Law 104–107 shall be deemed to include references\nto any hereinafter-enacted provision of law that is the same or substantially\nthe same as such section 571 or any subsection thereof.’’","original_source":{"page_or_item":"61 FR 64589 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(d)","sha256":"bbcc990f0250593bf0f990c75861cb29690edb1d1eadfed2783fe7dd4b149ff5","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1996-12-05/pdf/96-31164.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13028#sec1(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Judicial Review. This order is intended only to improve the internal\nmanagement of the Federal Government, and is not intended to create any\nright or benefit, substantive or procedural, enforceable by a party against\nthe United States, its agencies or instrumentalities, its officers or employees,\nor any other person.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"61 FR 64590 (PDF p. 2); Sec. 2","sha256":"bbcc990f0250593bf0f990c75861cb29690edb1d1eadfed2783fe7dd4b149ff5","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1996-12-05/pdf/96-31164.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13028#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"whole per-document Federal Register PDF (61 FR 64589)","sha256":"bbcc990f0250593bf0f990c75861cb29690edb1d1eadfed2783fe7dd4b149ff5","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1996-12-05/pdf/96-31164.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 6 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:13028"}
